{%- comment -%}
  snippets/structured-data.liquid
  ------------------------------------------------------------
  Sitewide JSON-LD structured data.
  Renders the correct schema graph based on request.page_type.
  Call once from layout/theme.liquid, right before </head>:

    {%- render 'structured-data' -%}

  Sections included:
    1. Homepage   -> Organization, WebSite, SearchAction, WebPage
    2. PDP         -> BreadcrumbList, WebPage/ItemPage, Product, AggregateOffer
    2b. PDP FAQ    -> FAQPage, built from product.metafields.Comergent.productFaqs (JSON list)
    3. PLP         -> BreadcrumbList, WebPage/CollectionPage, ItemList
    3b. PLP FAQ    -> FAQPage, from collection.metafields.custom.faqs (metaobject list)

  Notes:
  - Uses the Liquid `json` filter for all free-text fields (handles quotes/
    apostrophes/special chars safely) instead of manual escaping.
  - GTIN is mapped by barcode length rather than assuming gtin13.
  - aggregateRating / review only output when metafields are present.
  - FAQ schema only outputs when the corresponding metafield content is present,
    and should only be added if the FAQ content is visibly rendered on
    the page (see FAQ protocol notes below).
  - Before enabling on a client store, audit for duplicate schema from
    review apps (Judge.me, Yotpo, etc.) or AEO/SEO apps that may already
    output Product / FAQPage / Organization schema.
  - FIX: the PLP ItemList no longer embeds a full "@type": "Product" node
    per item. It previously reused the exact same @id as the PDP's real
    Product node ("{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}#product") but without
    offers/aggregateRating, which caused rating mismatches / missing-field
    warnings when parsers resolved the two same-@id nodes against each
    other. ItemList items now use the Google-recommended "position" + "url"
    pattern only. The PDP (section 2) remains the sole source of
    Product / offers / aggregateRating.
  - UPDATE: PLP FAQ (3b) now reads collection.metafields.custom.faqs, a
    list of metaobject references (each with question + answer fields),
    instead of a JSON list in custom.faq.
{%- endcomment -%}


{%- comment -%}
  ================= 1. HOMEPAGE =================
  LocalBusiness block below is OPTIONAL and only renders when
  shop.metafields.custom.local_business_type is populated (e.g. "Store",
  "ClothingStore", "JewelryStore" -- any valid schema.org LocalBusiness
  subtype). This keeps the block safely off for online-only stores with
  no physical storefront/showroom.

  Required metafields (Settings > Custom data > Shop, namespace: custom):
    local_business_type       (single line text)  e.g. "JewelryStore"
    local_business_street     (single line text)
    local_business_city       (single line text)
    local_business_region     (single line text)  e.g. state/province
    local_business_postal     (single line text)
    local_business_country    (single line text)  ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, e.g. "IN"
    local_business_lat        (number, decimal)    optional but recommended
    local_business_lng        (number, decimal)    optional but recommended
    local_business_hours      (single line text)   optional, schema.org format
                                 e.g. "Mo-Sa 10:00-19:00"
    local_business_pricerange (single line text)   optional, e.g. "$$"
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#organization",
      "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}",
      "logo": {
        "@type": "ImageObject",
        {%- if shop.brand and shop.brand.logo -%}
        "url": "{{ shop.brand.logo | image_url: width: 300 | prepend: 'https:' }}",
        "width": {{ shop.brand.logo.width }},
        "height": {{ shop.brand.logo.height }}
        {%- elsif settings.logo -%}
        "url": "{{ settings.logo | image_url: width: 300 | prepend: 'https:' }}",
        "width": 300,
        "height": 300
        {%- else -%}
        "url": "{{ 'logo.png' | asset_url | prepend: 'https:' }}",
        "width": 300,
        "height": 300
        {%- endif -%}
      }
      {%- comment -%}
        sameAs: add real brand social profile URLs, e.g.
        , "sameAs": ["https://www.instagram.com/yourbrand", "https://www.facebook.com/yourbrand"]
        Omit entirely if not available.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if shop.phone != blank or shop.email != blank -%},
      "contactPoint": [
        {
          "@type": "ContactPoint",
          "contactType": "customer service"
          {%- if shop.phone != blank -%},
          "telephone": {{ shop.phone | json }}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if shop.email != blank -%},
          "email": {{ shop.email | json }}
          {%- endif -%},
          "areaServed": "US",
          "availableLanguage": ["en"]
        }
      ]
      {%- endif -%}
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#website",
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}",
      "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
      "publisher": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#organization" },
      "inLanguage": "{{ request.locale.iso_code | default: 'en' }}",
      "potentialAction": {
        "@type": "SearchAction",
        "target": "{{ shop.url }}/search?q={search_term_string}",
        "query-input": "required name=search_term_string"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#webpage",
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}",
      "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
      "description": {{ page_description | default: shop.description | default: shop.name | strip_html | strip_newlines | truncate: 300 | json }},
      "isPartOf": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#website" },
      "about": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#organization" },
      "inLanguage": "{{ request.locale.iso_code | default: 'en' }}"
    }
    {%- if shop.metafields.custom.local_business_type != blank -%},
    {
      "@type": {{ shop.metafields.custom.local_business_type | json }},
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#localbusiness",
      "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}",
      "image": {
        {%- if shop.brand and shop.brand.logo -%}
        "@type": "ImageObject",
        "url": "{{ shop.brand.logo | image_url: width: 300 | prepend: 'https:' }}"
        {%- elsif settings.logo -%}
        "@type": "ImageObject",
        "url": "{{ settings.logo | image_url: width: 300 | prepend: 'https:' }}"
        {%- else -%}
        "@type": "ImageObject",
        "url": "{{ 'logo.png' | asset_url | prepend: 'https:' }}"
        {%- endif -%}
      },
      "parentOrganization": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#organization" }
      {%- if shop.phone != blank -%},
      "telephone": {{ shop.phone | json }}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if shop.email != blank -%},
      "email": {{ shop.email | json }}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if shop.metafields.custom.local_business_pricerange != blank -%},
      "priceRange": {{ shop.metafields.custom.local_business_pricerange.value | json }}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if shop.metafields.custom.local_business_street != blank -%},
      "address": {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        "streetAddress": {{ shop.metafields.custom.local_business_street.value | json }},
        "addressLocality": {{ shop.metafields.custom.local_business_city.value | json }},
        "addressRegion": {{ shop.metafields.custom.local_business_region.value | json }},
        "postalCode": {{ shop.metafields.custom.local_business_postal.value | json }},
        "addressCountry": {{ shop.metafields.custom.local_business_country.value | json }}
      }
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if shop.metafields.custom.local_business_lat != blank and shop.metafields.custom.local_business_lng != blank -%},
      "geo": {
        "@type": "GeoCoordinates",
        "latitude": {{ shop.metafields.custom.local_business_lat.value }},
        "longitude": {{ shop.metafields.custom.local_business_lng.value }}
      }
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if shop.metafields.custom.local_business_hours != blank -%},
      "openingHours": {{ shop.metafields.custom.local_business_hours.value | json }}
      {%- endif -%}
    }
    {%- endif -%}
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}


{%- comment -%} ================= 2. PRODUCT (PDP) ================= {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'product' and product -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}#breadcrumbs",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Home",
          "item": "{{ shop.url }}"
        }
        {%- if collection -%},
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": {{ collection.title | json }},
          "item": "{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}"
        }
        {%- endif -%},
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": {% if collection %}3{% else %}2{% endif %},
          "name": {{ product.title | json }},
          "item": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": ["WebPage", "ItemPage"],
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}#webpage",
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}",
      "name": {{ product.title | json }},
      "description": {{ product.description | strip_html | strip_newlines | truncate: 500 | json }},
      "inLanguage": "{{ request.locale.iso_code | default: 'en' }}",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@type": "WebSite",
        "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#website",
        "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
        "url": "{{ shop.url }}"
      },
      "breadcrumb": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}#breadcrumbs" },
      "mainEntity": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}#product" }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Product",
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}#product",
      "name": {{ product.title | json }},
      "description": {{ product.description | strip_html | strip_newlines | truncate: 1000 | json }},
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}",
      "image": [
        {%- for image in product.images limit: 5 -%}
        "{{ image | image_url: width: 1200 | prepend: 'https:' }}"{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      ],
      {%- if product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku != blank -%}
      "sku": {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku | json }},
      {%- endif -%}
      "brand": {
        "@type": "Brand",
        "name": {% if product.vendor != blank %}{{ product.vendor | json }}{% else %}{{ shop.name | json }}{% endif %}
      }
      {%- if product.collections.first -%},
      "category": {{ product.collections.first.title | json }}
      {%- endif -%},
      "offers": {
        "@type": "AggregateOffer",
        "priceCurrency": "{{ shop.currency }}",
        "offerCount": {{ product.variants.size }},
        "lowPrice": {{ product.price_min | times: 0.01 | round: 2 }},
        "highPrice": {{ product.price_max | times: 0.01 | round: 2 }},
        "offers": [
          {%- for v in product.variants -%}
          {
            "@type": "Offer",
            "url": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}?variant={{ v.id }}",
            "priceCurrency": "{{ shop.currency }}",
            "price": {{ v.price | times: 0.01 | round: 2 }},
            "availability": "https://schema.org/{% if v.available %}InStock{% else %}OutOfStock{% endif %}"
            {%- if v.sku != blank -%},"sku": {{ v.sku | json }}{%- endif -%}
            {%- assign bc = v.barcode | strip -%}
            {%- if bc != blank -%}
              {%- assign bc_len = bc | size -%}
              {%- if bc_len == 14 -%},"gtin14": {{ bc | json }}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if bc_len == 13 -%},"gtin13": {{ bc | json }}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if bc_len == 12 -%},"gtin12": {{ bc | json }}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if bc_len == 8 -%},"gtin8": {{ bc | json }}{%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%},
            "itemCondition": "https://schema.org/NewCondition",
            "seller": {
              "@type": "Organization",
              "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#organization",
              "name": {{ shop.name | json }}
            }
          }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
          {%- endfor -%}
        ]
      }
      {%- if product.metafields.reviews.rating_value != blank and product.metafields.reviews.rating_count != blank -%},
      "aggregateRating": {
        "@type": "AggregateRating",
        "ratingValue": {{ product.metafields.reviews.rating_value }},
        "ratingCount": {{ product.metafields.reviews.rating_count }},
        "bestRating": 5,
        "worstRating": 1
      }
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if product.metafields.reviews.recent_json != blank -%},
      "review": {{ product.metafields.reviews.recent_json }}
      {%- endif -%}
    }
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}


{%- comment -%} ================= 2b. PDP FAQ (Comergent.productFaqs metafield) ================= {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Metafield: product.metafields.Comergent.productFaqs
  Type: JSON list of objects, each shaped like {"question": "...", "answer": "..."}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'product' and product.metafields.Comergent.productFaqs.value != blank -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}#faq",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- for faq in product.metafields.Comergent.productFaqs.value -%}
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": {{ faq.question | strip_html | strip_newlines | json }},
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": {{ faq.answer | strip_html | strip_newlines | json }}
      }
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}


{%- comment -%} ================= 3. COLLECTION (PLP) ================= {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  FIXED: itemListElement entries used to embed a full "@type": "Product"
  node reusing the PDP's exact @id ("...#product") but without offers/
  aggregateRating. That @id collision between an incomplete collection-page
  stub and the complete PDP node is what caused wrong/missing aggregate
  rating results. Per Google's guidance for listing/carousel pages, each
  ListItem now carries "position" + "url" + "name" + "image" directly on
  itself (no nested "item" object, no "@type": "Product", no @id) -- so
  the listing page still surfaces product name/image for rich results
  without ever declaring a competing Product entity. The PDP (section 2)
  stays the only place Product / offers / aggregateRating are declared.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'collection' and collection -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}#breadcrumbs",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Home",
          "item": "{{ shop.url }}"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": {{ collection.title | json }},
          "item": "{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": ["WebPage", "CollectionPage"],
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}#webpage",
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}",
      "name": {{ collection.title | json }},
      "description": {{ collection.description | strip_html | strip_newlines | truncate: 500 | json }},
      "isPartOf": {
        "@type": "WebSite",
        "@id": "{{ shop.url }}#website",
        "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
        "url": "{{ shop.url }}"
      },
      "inLanguage": "{{ request.locale.iso_code | default: 'en' }}",
      "breadcrumb": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}#breadcrumbs" },
      "about": {
        "@type": "Thing",
        "name": {{ collection.title | json }}
      },
      "mainEntity": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}#itemlist" }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}#itemlist",
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}",
      "numberOfItems": {{ collection.products_count }},
      "itemListElement": [
        {%- for product in collection.products -%}
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": {{ forloop.index }},
          "url": "{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}",
          "name": {{ product.title | json }}
          {%- if product.featured_image -%},
          "image": "{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 1024 | prepend: 'https:' }}"
          {%- endif -%}
        }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}


{%- comment -%} ================= 3b. PLP FAQ (metaobject list: custom.faqs) ================= {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Metafield: collection.metafields.custom.faqs (namespace: custom, key: faqs)
  Type: List of metaobject references (definition: "Collection FAQ").
  Metaobject definition "Collection FAQ" (type: collection_faq) fields:
    - question  (single line text)
    - answers   (rich text)
  `metafield_text` converts the rich text answer to plain text, so the
  schema never contains the rich text JSON. If the field keys are ever
  renamed in the definition, update `faq.question` / `faq.answers` below.

  Requirements:
    - Storefront access enabled on the Collection FAQ metaobject definition
    - Entries set to Active (not draft)
    - FAQ content should also be visibly rendered on the collection page
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign plp_faqs = collection.metafields.custom.faqs.value -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'collection' and plp_faqs != blank -%}
  {%- assign faq_started = false -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}#faq",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- for faq in plp_faqs -%}
      {%- assign faq_q = faq.question | metafield_text | strip_html | strip_newlines | strip -%}
      {%- assign faq_a = faq.answers | metafield_text | strip_html | strip_newlines | strip -%}
      {%- if faq_q != blank and faq_a != blank -%}
        {%- if faq_started -%},{%- endif -%}
        {%- assign faq_started = true -%}
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": {{ faq_q | json }},
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": {{ faq_a | json }}
      }
    }
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}
